<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/cursor') %>
  <%- include('partials/nav') %>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="pitch-hero">
    <div class="pitch-hero-inner reveal">
      <span class="pitch-hero-badge">Feature Film &middot; Comedy</span>
      <h1 class="pitch-hero-title">Ripples of<br>Easdale</h1>
      <p class="pitch-hero-byline">In Development</p>
      <p class="pitch-hero-logline">A broke, hot-headed dairy farmer takes on his smug rival &mdash; a five-time champion turned local tycoon &mdash; at Scotland's legendary stone-skimming championship to save his family farm, only to discover the sport's oldest myths about bending time might just be true.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Facts -->
  <div class="pitch-facts">
    <div class="pitch-fact">
      <span class="pitch-fact-label">Format</span>
      <span class="pitch-fact-value">Feature Film</span>
    </div>
    <div class="pitch-fact">
      <span class="pitch-fact-label">Genre</span>
      <span class="pitch-fact-value">Underdog Comedy</span>
    </div>
    <div class="pitch-fact">
      <span class="pitch-fact-label">Setting</span>
      <span class="pitch-fact-value">Isle of Easdale, Scotland</span>
    </div>
    <div class="pitch-fact">
      <span class="pitch-fact-label">Status</span>
      <span class="pitch-fact-value">In Development</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Synopsis -->
  <section class="pitch-section">
    <div class="pitch-section-inner reveal">
      <span class="pitch-eyebrow">The Story</span>
      <h2 class="pitch-heading">Big, dumb, glorious spectacle &mdash; poured into the smallest village in Scotland.</h2>
      <div class="pitch-body">
        <p>Finn McCreadie's dairy farm is going under, and the man buying up every business in Easdale to get his hands on it is the same smug rival who's beaten him at the village's legendary stone-skimming championship five years running. So Finn does the only sensible thing: trains with his hermit uncle, who lives in a hut made of stones and insists that skipping a rock right doesn't just win trophies &mdash; it bends time itself.</p>
        <p>What starts as a village grudge match escalates into something much bigger, much stranger, and much funnier &mdash; equal parts underdog sports comedy and self-aware, over-the-top spectacle, played completely straight by everyone in it. Ripples of Easdale is set against the real Isle of Easdale, home to the genuine World Stone Skimming Championships held there every year &mdash; giving the film a built-in, ready-made piece of Scottish culture to hang its comedy on.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pitch-comps">
        <span class="pitch-comp-chip">In the vein of Eddie the Eagle</span>
        <span class="pitch-comp-chip">In the vein of Hot Fuzz</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Characters -->
  <section class="pitch-characters">
    <div class="pitch-characters-inner reveal">
      <span class="pitch-eyebrow">Who's In It</span>
      <h2 class="pitch-heading">Character Breakdown</h2>
      <div class="pitch-characters-grid">
        <div class="pitch-character">
          <span class="pitch-character-name">Finn McCreadie</span>
          <p class="pitch-character-desc">Broke, furious, and hurling milk bottles at trees before breakfast. Grandson of the village's legendary skimming champion, and about to find out if greatness runs in the blood.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pitch-character">
          <span class="pitch-character-name">Callum &ldquo;The Cannon&rdquo; McDougall</span>
          <p class="pitch-character-desc">Five-time champion, dairy tycoon, Bond villain with a fur-lined jacket. Turned the village's proudest tradition into a corporate victory lap &mdash; and he's not finished yet.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pitch-character">
          <span class="pitch-character-name">Rab McCreadie</span>
          <p class="pitch-character-desc">Finn's unhinged hermit uncle, living in a stone hut and training Finn through barefoot milk runs and forced Enya listening sessions. Funnier for being dead serious about every word of it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pitch-character">
          <span class="pitch-character-name">Mairi MacLean</span>
          <p class="pitch-character-desc">Village pub owner and quantum physicist who came home instead of chasing a career at CERN. The one person in Easdale who might actually be able to explain what's happening.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Statement -->
  <section class="pitch-quote">
    <div class="pitch-quote-inner reveal">
      <span class="pitch-quote-mark">&ldquo;</span>
      <p class="pitch-quote-text">Ripples of Easdale takes a real Scottish tradition and asks what happens if you point a blockbuster camera at it &mdash; sweeping shots, a swelling score, and a village pub, all played dead straight. It's a love letter to community over corporate creep, and to the idea that the biggest stories can come from the smallest places.</p>
      <cite class="pitch-quote-cite">Alasdair Braxton, Writer</cite>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="pitch-cta">
    <div class="pitch-cta-inner reveal">
      <h2 class="pitch-cta-heading">Read the Full Script</h2>
      <p class="pitch-cta-text">Ripples of Easdale is currently in development and seeking production partners. Get in touch to request the full script.</p>
      <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>?subject=Ripples%20of%20Easdale%20%E2%80%94%20Script%20Request" class="pitch-cta-btn">Request the Script</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
  <%- include('partials/scripts') %>
</body>
</html>
